1
00:00:14,560 --> 00:00:16,560
[theme song in Japanese playing]

2
00:01:37,520 --> 00:01:39,900
SPARKS OF TOMORROW

3
00:01:39,980 --> 00:01:43,940
EPISODE 2: THE MYSTERIES OF THE CATALOG

4
00:01:44,030 --> 00:01:45,620
[coughing]

5
00:01:45,700 --> 00:01:47,790
- [Inako] Is that incense?
- [Kihachi] What's going on?

6
00:01:49,700 --> 00:01:51,240
I found you at last, 

7
00:01:51,330 --> 00:01:52,540
my wife.

8
00:01:52,620 --> 00:01:54,540
[screams]

9
00:01:55,830 --> 00:01:57,580
- No! Not you!
- [groans]

10
00:01:57,670 --> 00:01:59,510
I came for my darling wife!

11
00:01:59,580 --> 00:02:02,000
And the 20th Century Electrical Catalog!

12
00:02:02,090 --> 00:02:03,380
[gasps] Catalog?

13
00:02:03,460 --> 00:02:04,880
Wha-wha-what do you mean?

14
00:02:04,970 --> 00:02:07,260
- I'm not your wife!
- Just that. You are to be my wife.

15
00:02:07,340 --> 00:02:09,090
[gasps] Your wife?

16
00:02:09,180 --> 00:02:11,390
Wait, is this guy really your fiancé?

17
00:02:11,470 --> 00:02:14,310
[Inako] Obviously not!
I have no idea what he's talking about.

18
00:02:14,390 --> 00:02:15,770
Of course you don't.

19
00:02:15,850 --> 00:02:19,310
It has only been a short time
since I received your father's blessing.

20
00:02:20,520 --> 00:02:22,770
Look at you, so happy you can't speak.

21
00:02:22,860 --> 00:02:24,030
I get it.

22
00:02:24,110 --> 00:02:27,240
It's a great honor
to be betrothed to me, after all.

23
00:02:27,320 --> 00:02:30,070
Yosuke Mizoe. The heir to the Mizoe Firm!

24
00:02:30,160 --> 00:02:31,410
I refuse!

25
00:02:31,490 --> 00:02:33,580
[Yosuke scoffs] What does that mean?

26
00:02:33,660 --> 00:02:36,330
It almost sounds like
you don't want to be my wife.

27
00:02:36,410 --> 00:02:38,660
I don't want to be your wife! I refuse!

28
00:02:38,750 --> 00:02:39,920
- [yelps] What?
- [power sparks]

29
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:42,670
- I refuse!
- [whimpers]

30
00:02:43,340 --> 00:02:45,090
[strained] Enough playing around.

31
00:02:45,170 --> 00:02:47,010
- Give me the catalog!
- No! No!

32
00:02:47,090 --> 00:02:48,550
- Let go!
- [straining]

33
00:02:48,630 --> 00:02:51,300
- Hey! Knock it off! You'll tear it!
- [groaning]

34
00:02:51,390 --> 00:02:52,640
[yelps]

35
00:02:54,680 --> 00:02:56,470
- [crashing echoing]
- [inaudible]

36
00:02:56,560 --> 00:02:57,810
[gasps]

37
00:02:58,310 --> 00:03:00,730
Ugh! What are you doing, 
you pompous creep?

38
00:03:00,810 --> 00:03:02,730
- [grunting]
- [rattling]

39
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:05,490
[Kihachi] Get out of here!

40
00:03:05,570 --> 00:03:07,740
[Yosuke] You're too late, kid!

41
00:03:08,700 --> 00:03:09,870
[energy crackling]

42
00:03:09,950 --> 00:03:11,120
- [gasps]
- [aide grunts]

43
00:03:11,200 --> 00:03:12,200
Mr. Mizoe!

44
00:03:12,780 --> 00:03:13,820
[Yosuke sighs]

45
00:03:14,910 --> 00:03:16,370
What… [gulps]

46
00:03:17,830 --> 00:03:20,040
- No, don't hurt him! [gasps]
- [aide] Sorry, Miss.

47
00:03:24,040 --> 00:03:25,000
[Inari squeaks]

48
00:03:25,590 --> 00:03:27,590
My hair's ruined!

49
00:03:27,670 --> 00:03:28,630
[grumbling]

50
00:03:28,720 --> 00:03:30,180
- Aah!
- [aide] Hmm.

51
00:03:32,260 --> 00:03:34,180
[Yajiro gasps]

52
00:03:35,260 --> 00:03:36,300
[whimpers softly]

53
00:03:36,430 --> 00:03:37,680
Do not be alarmed.

54
00:03:39,560 --> 00:03:40,440
[Yajiro] Kihachi!

55
00:03:41,020 --> 00:03:42,520
[Bunshichi gasps]

56
00:03:48,940 --> 00:03:51,650
Damn it! Who was that brat?

57
00:03:51,740 --> 00:03:54,740
- If he's using electricity… [growls]
- What's the plan now?

58
00:03:54,820 --> 00:03:57,240
- Sir, what should we do next?
- [yells] Aah! We're done here!

59
00:03:57,330 --> 00:03:59,460
- Get me out of this place at once!
- [static crackles]

60
00:03:59,540 --> 00:04:01,710
I've got you, K-K-Kihachi!

61
00:04:01,790 --> 00:04:05,130
[groans] The catalog…
Did he get the catalog?

62
00:04:05,210 --> 00:04:07,210
[grunts] Damn it!

63
00:04:07,300 --> 00:04:09,300
- [engine revving]
- [steam hissing]

64
00:04:11,720 --> 00:04:13,010
[lively music playing]

65
00:04:14,010 --> 00:04:15,390
[grunting]

66
00:04:18,680 --> 00:04:19,970
[Kihachi] Stop that car!

67
00:04:20,060 --> 00:04:21,810
- [Yosuke yelps]
- [Inako groans]

68
00:04:23,770 --> 00:04:25,940
[Yosuke] You don't know when to give up, 
do you, Sparky?

69
00:04:26,020 --> 00:04:28,150
[Kihachi] Give me the catalog, 
you white-haired freak!

70
00:04:28,230 --> 00:04:29,520
[creaking]

71
00:04:30,110 --> 00:04:31,650
[both straining]

72
00:04:31,740 --> 00:04:34,700
Mr. Sakamoto! Grab it! Here!

73
00:04:34,780 --> 00:04:36,490
- [Yosuke] Know your place!
- [Inako gasps]

74
00:04:36,570 --> 00:04:38,320
[yells]

75
00:04:38,410 --> 00:04:40,950
Blunt force is all
your inventions are good for.

76
00:04:41,040 --> 00:04:43,250
You'll never be half the man he was.

77
00:04:43,330 --> 00:04:44,580
Hold on back there.

78
00:04:44,670 --> 00:04:45,840
I'm giving it some steam.

79
00:04:45,920 --> 00:04:47,090
[Yosuke] Do it!

80
00:04:48,840 --> 00:04:49,840
[Kihachi gasps]

81
00:04:53,220 --> 00:04:55,140
- [yelps]
- [Yosuke chuckles]

82
00:04:55,220 --> 00:04:56,930
See ya around, kid.

83
00:04:57,010 --> 00:04:59,010
Please stop the car and let me out.

84
00:04:59,600 --> 00:05:01,940
That's enough.
As a wife of the Mizoe family, 

85
00:05:02,020 --> 00:05:04,110
you will cease this disgraceful behavior!

86
00:05:04,690 --> 00:05:07,690
Or do you wish to bring more shame
to your family's name?

87
00:05:07,770 --> 00:05:08,770
[Inako sighs]

88
00:05:08,860 --> 00:05:10,780
[Kihachi struggling]

89
00:05:10,860 --> 00:05:12,070
Damn it!

90
00:05:12,150 --> 00:05:15,280
[sobs] Why did he have
to take the catalog?

91
00:05:15,360 --> 00:05:17,280
- [people exclaiming]
- [man 1] A steam pipe burst!

92
00:05:17,370 --> 00:05:20,290
[man 2] Quickly! We need to contact
the Mizoe firm and report it!

93
00:05:21,660 --> 00:05:23,040
[man 3] Hey, hey! Out of the way!

94
00:05:24,460 --> 00:05:27,210
I need to change routes.
There seems to be an accident ahead.

95
00:05:27,290 --> 00:05:29,250
I don't care, just drive!

96
00:05:29,340 --> 00:05:31,340
Damn it. [growls]

97
00:05:31,420 --> 00:05:32,500
[Inako] Hmm.

98
00:05:33,920 --> 00:05:35,880
[lively music continues]

99
00:05:41,220 --> 00:05:42,970
[inhales]

100
00:05:43,060 --> 00:05:44,900
[exhales]

101
00:05:44,980 --> 00:05:46,360
So, Sparky's all grown up.

102
00:05:46,440 --> 00:05:48,690
I never expected to see him again.

103
00:05:48,770 --> 00:05:50,060
[chuckles]

104
00:05:50,150 --> 00:05:51,030
[gasps happily]

105
00:05:51,110 --> 00:05:52,530
More importantly…

106
00:05:52,610 --> 00:05:54,860
- It's time. Give it to me!
- No!

107
00:05:54,940 --> 00:05:57,860
[Yosuke] You will do as you're told.
Do not dare defy me!

108
00:05:57,950 --> 00:05:59,080
Please don't come any closer.

109
00:05:59,160 --> 00:06:01,410
- Or I swear I'll throw it!
- Stop this foolishness at once!

110
00:06:01,490 --> 00:06:04,410
Gah! There's smoke in my eyes! [screams]

111
00:06:04,500 --> 00:06:05,830
Mr. Mizoe! [grunts]

112
00:06:06,410 --> 00:06:07,620
[gasps]

113
00:06:08,120 --> 00:06:09,160
[aide sighs]

114
00:06:11,540 --> 00:06:13,420
- [panting]
- [Kengo] Yosuke?

115
00:06:13,510 --> 00:06:15,890
[Yosuke] No! The catalog!

116
00:06:15,970 --> 00:06:17,760
- The catalog?
- [Yosuke groans] Get it!

117
00:06:17,840 --> 00:06:18,930
Right!

118
00:06:20,050 --> 00:06:21,760
- [sighs shakily]
- [music fades]

119
00:06:22,930 --> 00:06:24,260
I'll go help them.

120
00:06:24,350 --> 00:06:26,440
- [murmuring]
- [man 1] What do you think they're up to?

121
00:06:26,520 --> 00:06:28,650
[man 2] Cooling off
from this heat, I'd say.

122
00:06:28,730 --> 00:06:31,190
Sister-in-law, 
please keep an eye on my darling girl.

123
00:06:32,320 --> 00:06:34,450
You couldn't deliver it to Mr. Sakamoto?

124
00:06:35,030 --> 00:06:37,950
[man 2] That's the right idea, fellas!
Keep it up!

125
00:06:38,530 --> 00:06:39,860
[Bunshichi sighs]

126
00:06:39,950 --> 00:06:42,450
Don't just sit there, Kihachi.
Help me clean this up.

127
00:06:42,530 --> 00:06:44,950
Uh… Hey, are you okay, Kihachi?

128
00:06:45,040 --> 00:06:46,540
[Kihachi sniffles]

129
00:06:46,620 --> 00:06:50,460
That pompous jerk scared the hell
out of me, barging in like that.

130
00:06:50,540 --> 00:06:52,960
[sobbing] And he took the catalog.

131
00:06:53,040 --> 00:06:55,290
I had it, I finally had it.

132
00:06:55,380 --> 00:06:57,470
[sobs] How could I
lose it again like that?

133
00:06:57,550 --> 00:06:58,970
Kihachi.

134
00:06:59,970 --> 00:07:01,680
So… now what?

135
00:07:02,300 --> 00:07:03,340
[Kihachi] Damn it!

136
00:07:04,390 --> 00:07:05,520
[sniffles]

137
00:07:05,600 --> 00:07:07,190
I've always been a coward.

138
00:07:07,770 --> 00:07:09,730
And now I always will be.

139
00:07:10,270 --> 00:07:11,900
[all panting and wheezing]

140
00:07:11,980 --> 00:07:14,320
I can't go on! [gasping]

141
00:07:14,400 --> 00:07:15,900
- [aide] Mr. Mizoe!
- What?

142
00:07:17,740 --> 00:07:21,540
[screaming]

143
00:07:21,610 --> 00:07:23,610
[waterbirds calling]

144
00:07:33,670 --> 00:07:34,630
[Noriko] Father!

145
00:07:35,130 --> 00:07:38,050
How could you promise
to marry Inako to Yosuke?

146
00:07:38,130 --> 00:07:40,920
[Mr. Momokawa] How can I refuse
the heir of the Mizoe firm?

147
00:07:41,010 --> 00:07:45,510
Marrying Inako into the Mizoe family
will keep our debt collectors at bay.

148
00:07:45,600 --> 00:07:48,390
Our sake brewery is
in danger of bankruptcy.

149
00:07:48,480 --> 00:07:50,650
- What of our family legacy?
- [Noriko gasps]

150
00:07:50,730 --> 00:07:52,940
[Mr. Momokawa]
Do you want to lose the brewery, Noriko?

151
00:07:53,020 --> 00:07:58,440
Of course not. But that still doesn't
justify locking Inako in the storehouse.

152
00:07:58,530 --> 00:08:01,910
Can you tell me you honestly believe
there is another family out there

153
00:08:01,990 --> 00:08:04,580
who will accept Inako as a bride?

154
00:08:04,660 --> 00:08:07,460
The girl can't even serve
a proper cup of tea.

155
00:08:07,540 --> 00:08:08,710
[sighs]

156
00:08:08,790 --> 00:08:10,210
[clattering]

157
00:08:10,290 --> 00:08:14,460
[Mr. Momokawa] Regardless of how you feel, 
daughters should obey their father's will.

158
00:08:14,540 --> 00:08:17,130
Father, Inako is only 15 years old.

159
00:08:17,210 --> 00:08:19,710
There is still so much
she has yet to learn and experience.

160
00:08:23,050 --> 00:08:25,180
[Inari squeaking frantically]

161
00:08:25,260 --> 00:08:27,760
[Kihachi yelps]
[squealing]

162
00:08:29,350 --> 00:08:30,770
[shamisen playing]

163
00:08:37,900 --> 00:08:39,030
- [Inari squeaks]
- Huh?

164
00:08:39,110 --> 00:08:41,150
- [squeaks]
- [Inako] Hi, Inari.

165
00:08:44,360 --> 00:08:45,530
[squeaks]

166
00:08:45,620 --> 00:08:48,920
- [squeaking softly]
- Aw, thank you, Inari.

167
00:08:48,990 --> 00:08:52,950
Father was very angry with me when
I told him I didn't wanna get married, 

168
00:08:53,040 --> 00:08:54,420
so he locked me in here.

169
00:08:55,250 --> 00:08:57,380
I understand where he's coming from.

170
00:08:57,460 --> 00:09:01,760
If things stay as they are, the brewery, 
my mother's legacy, will collapse.

171
00:09:02,260 --> 00:09:06,430
Inari, I know I can save everything
if I marry Mr. Mizoe. [sighs]

172
00:09:07,010 --> 00:09:08,550
It's always been like this.

173
00:09:09,060 --> 00:09:12,440
First, my father gets angry at me
for disobeying him, 

174
00:09:12,520 --> 00:09:14,440
then he locks me in the storeroom.

175
00:09:14,520 --> 00:09:19,150
After a while, 
he comes back and apologizes.

176
00:09:20,020 --> 00:09:22,060
And after all that…

177
00:09:22,150 --> 00:09:24,320
[Kihachi] Are you really
gonna marry that guy?

178
00:09:24,900 --> 00:09:26,070
[Inako] Mr. Sakamoto?

179
00:09:26,160 --> 00:09:27,700
[Kihachi grunts]

180
00:09:30,030 --> 00:09:32,240
Mr. Sakamoto, why are you here?

181
00:09:32,330 --> 00:09:34,000
Just call me Kihachi.

182
00:09:34,080 --> 00:09:35,290
Kihachi?

183
00:09:35,370 --> 00:09:38,790
You mentioned Momokawa Sake Brewery
in the recording yesterday, 

184
00:09:38,880 --> 00:09:40,470
so I figured you'd be here.

185
00:09:40,550 --> 00:09:44,680
You can't be here! If anyone sees you, 
you'll be in big trouble.

186
00:09:44,760 --> 00:09:48,100
It's worth the risk. There's something
I need to know about the catalog.

187
00:09:48,180 --> 00:09:50,730
Huh? Oh, that's perfect.
It's right here!

188
00:09:50,810 --> 00:09:53,230
Huh? Wait. Didn't he try
to take that from you?

189
00:09:54,310 --> 00:09:56,810
[Inako] He tried. But I hid it.

190
00:09:58,020 --> 00:10:00,440
THE 20TH CENTURY ELECTRICAL CATALOG

191
00:10:01,150 --> 00:10:02,110
[Kihachi] Um…

192
00:10:02,780 --> 00:10:04,160
[Inako] Hmm!

193
00:10:04,240 --> 00:10:07,160
[Yosuke panting and wheezing]

194
00:10:07,740 --> 00:10:09,620
Izo! Kuga! Grab it!

195
00:10:10,620 --> 00:10:11,500
[both yell]

196
00:10:14,080 --> 00:10:16,170
[groaning]

197
00:10:17,710 --> 00:10:20,090
Give it here! Hand it over!

198
00:10:20,170 --> 00:10:21,420
Gah!

199
00:10:21,500 --> 00:10:22,670
Huh? [gasps]

200
00:10:23,340 --> 00:10:24,670
[Kengo] It's empty.

201
00:10:24,760 --> 00:10:25,760
[Yosuke shudders]

202
00:10:25,840 --> 00:10:28,430
My sweet darling girl, 
what have you done now?

203
00:10:28,510 --> 00:10:29,550
NUMBER 11

204
00:10:29,640 --> 00:10:31,180
[Kihachi] There's no doubt.

205
00:10:31,260 --> 00:10:34,430
This is definitely the catalog
my older brother gave me.

206
00:10:37,690 --> 00:10:39,690
[wistful music playing]

207
00:10:43,070 --> 00:10:45,570
- [Inako] Your brother gave this to you?
- [Seiroku] Kihachi.

208
00:10:46,150 --> 00:10:48,820
[Kihachi] He said the 20th century
would be the Age of Electricity, 

209
00:10:49,410 --> 00:10:51,910
and to put all my ideas
for inventions in here.

210
00:10:52,740 --> 00:10:55,330
Then he took me
to the Industrial Exhibition.

211
00:10:56,160 --> 00:10:59,370
Ever since that day, 
my head has been swimming

212
00:10:59,460 --> 00:11:02,000
with all sorts of visions of the future.

213
00:11:04,250 --> 00:11:06,880
NUMBER 2, ELECTRICITY

214
00:11:08,130 --> 00:11:12,050
I can tell you really look up to your
big brother by how you talk about him.

215
00:11:12,140 --> 00:11:13,810
[gasps and grunts]

216
00:11:13,890 --> 00:11:16,350
He said we'd bring in
the Age of Electricity.

217
00:11:16,430 --> 00:11:20,140
He took the catalog with him to war, 
and never came back.

218
00:11:20,940 --> 00:11:22,650
Can't believe I trusted him.

219
00:11:23,480 --> 00:11:25,520
I'd never look up to someone like that.

220
00:11:26,110 --> 00:11:28,240
But now you finally
have the catalog again!

221
00:11:28,320 --> 00:11:31,950
- Don't take me for a fool.
- [gasps] I'm not… trying to.

222
00:11:32,030 --> 00:11:33,450
You just show up out of the blue

223
00:11:33,530 --> 00:11:36,120
and tell me your sister's
had this the whole time?

224
00:11:36,700 --> 00:11:38,870
And it's been torn in half!

225
00:11:38,960 --> 00:11:40,800
My brother went
to a vocational school in Shiga.

226
00:11:40,870 --> 00:11:42,710
Where would he have even met your sister?

227
00:11:42,790 --> 00:11:44,880
Okay, they knew each other, so what?

228
00:11:45,590 --> 00:11:47,630
He knew her well enough
to entrust her with this?

229
00:11:47,710 --> 00:11:49,250
What's that mean?

230
00:11:49,340 --> 00:11:52,260
Are you trying to suggest
that my sister is being dishonest?

231
00:11:52,340 --> 00:11:57,010
- No. But you gotta admit it's suspicious.
- You need to have a little faith!

232
00:11:57,100 --> 00:12:00,810
Believing in one another
is what protects the bonds of humanity.

233
00:12:01,850 --> 00:12:02,810
[Kihachi] Huh.

234
00:12:03,440 --> 00:12:04,770
Whatever.

235
00:12:04,860 --> 00:12:06,450
[scoffs] I'm out of here.

236
00:12:08,150 --> 00:12:10,440
- [squeaking]
- [clattering]

237
00:12:11,150 --> 00:12:12,480
Okay, bye.

238
00:12:12,570 --> 00:12:16,070
You have to hurry. My father will be
coming back any minute to check on me

239
00:12:16,160 --> 00:12:18,580
and I don't think
he'd be too happy finding you here.

240
00:12:18,660 --> 00:12:20,040
[Kihachi grunting]

241
00:12:20,620 --> 00:12:22,620
- It's… it's stuck!
- Hmm?

242
00:12:22,710 --> 00:12:25,340
[Kihachi] Useless piece of crap! Damn it!

243
00:12:25,420 --> 00:12:26,800
[groaning]

244
00:12:27,920 --> 00:12:30,380
[Kihachi and Inako straining]

245
00:12:30,470 --> 00:12:31,390
[squeaks]

246
00:12:32,930 --> 00:12:34,930
[both groaning]

247
00:12:40,890 --> 00:12:42,980
- [groans] I did it!
- [Inako sighs]

248
00:12:43,060 --> 00:12:44,600
[both panting]

249
00:12:44,690 --> 00:12:49,570
- You… only did it… because I helped you.
- [Kihachi yelps]

250
00:12:49,650 --> 00:12:51,240
[both groan]

251
00:12:51,320 --> 00:12:53,610
[Inako] I should… get back inside.

252
00:12:54,570 --> 00:12:56,070
[wind gusting]

253
00:12:56,160 --> 00:12:57,870
Sure you wanna do that?

254
00:12:57,950 --> 00:12:58,990
[Inako] Huh?

255
00:13:00,040 --> 00:13:01,080
I…

256
00:13:02,620 --> 00:13:05,210
I have to go back and marry that man.

257
00:13:06,080 --> 00:13:08,500
Do you actually want to marry him?

258
00:13:08,590 --> 00:13:09,590
No.

259
00:13:10,420 --> 00:13:13,260
But my father told me I have to.

260
00:13:13,880 --> 00:13:15,340
- [Kihachi] Hey, Bug.
- Huh?

261
00:13:16,590 --> 00:13:17,470
Come on.

262
00:13:20,850 --> 00:13:21,850
[Inako] Huh?

263
00:13:30,360 --> 00:13:33,030
[Kengo sighs] You've changed, Yosuke.

264
00:13:33,110 --> 00:13:35,820
Since when did you start
wearing such flashy suits?

265
00:13:35,910 --> 00:13:37,410
Save the reunion for later.

266
00:13:37,990 --> 00:13:41,450
All right. At least tell me
why you want the catalog, then.

267
00:13:41,540 --> 00:13:45,500
You really have no idea
what that book's true value is, do you?

268
00:13:45,580 --> 00:13:46,670
What are you talking about?

269
00:13:46,750 --> 00:13:48,000
[chuckles]

270
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:50,420
Izo! Hurry up!

271
00:13:51,500 --> 00:13:53,290
[Inako] Wow!

272
00:13:56,880 --> 00:14:00,340
Man, helping you
has been one hell of a distraction.

273
00:14:01,810 --> 00:14:03,440
[gasps happily]

274
00:14:04,640 --> 00:14:06,060
[wind gusting]

275
00:14:06,850 --> 00:14:08,180
Kihachi?

276
00:14:08,270 --> 00:14:10,110
- Uh…
- [Inako] Thank you for everything.

277
00:14:15,190 --> 00:14:18,110
- [Noriko] Inako?
- [Mr. Momokawa] Hmm? Inako!

278
00:14:18,200 --> 00:14:20,040
- Quick! Someone help!
- Father, I feel so dizzy!

279
00:14:20,120 --> 00:14:21,450
- [both yelp]
- Oh, goodness.

280
00:14:21,530 --> 00:14:23,450
- Noriko, get off of me.
- [Noriko whimpers]

281
00:14:23,540 --> 00:14:24,540
[both struggling]

282
00:14:24,620 --> 00:14:27,210
- Oh, no! Are you all right, Father?
- [Mr. Momokawa] Let me up! Hey!

283
00:14:27,290 --> 00:14:28,500
Someone! Come quick!

284
00:14:28,580 --> 00:14:31,080
- He's seen us! Kihachi, run.
- [Mr. Momokawa] Noriko, get off me!

285
00:14:31,170 --> 00:14:33,170
[Inako] If he catches you, 
you're in trouble.

286
00:14:33,250 --> 00:14:34,920
- Inako, wait!
- [Noriko] Father!

287
00:14:35,010 --> 00:14:37,510
- [Inako] What are you doing? What's that?
- It's a kite.

288
00:14:37,590 --> 00:14:38,840
I can use it to fly away.

289
00:14:39,430 --> 00:14:41,810
Wow! Can you really fly that?

290
00:14:41,890 --> 00:14:43,980
[Kihachi] Theoretically, yes.

291
00:14:44,060 --> 00:14:47,230
But if I'm being honest…
I doubt it'll work.

292
00:14:47,310 --> 00:14:49,600
[Inako] What do you mean? You invented it!

293
00:14:49,690 --> 00:14:52,070
I never thought I'd actually
have to use this thing.

294
00:14:52,150 --> 00:14:57,110
- Get them down!
- My inventions aren't half as good as his.

295
00:14:57,900 --> 00:14:59,190
It's not gonna fly.

296
00:14:59,280 --> 00:15:01,620
- [determined music playing]
- [Kihachi gasping shakily]

297
00:15:03,370 --> 00:15:05,830
- Hey! Stop! What are you doing?
- I believe in you!

298
00:15:05,910 --> 00:15:07,580
- What? [wails]
- Here we go!

299
00:15:07,660 --> 00:15:09,830
- [Inako yelling]
- Hey! No, no, no! Wait, wait! Stop!

300
00:15:09,920 --> 00:15:12,460
We're gonna fall, Bug, stop!
We're gonna fall! No!

301
00:15:12,540 --> 00:15:16,000
- Yah!
- What do you mean, "yah"? I said no! Stop!

302
00:15:18,380 --> 00:15:20,010
[Inako panting]

303
00:15:21,890 --> 00:15:22,810
Jump!

304
00:15:25,720 --> 00:15:27,010
[man] Young miss!

305
00:15:27,850 --> 00:15:28,940
[men yelp]

306
00:15:29,020 --> 00:15:30,480
[Kihachi yelling]

307
00:15:35,400 --> 00:15:37,490
[screaming]

308
00:15:41,280 --> 00:15:43,700
[screaming]

309
00:15:51,670 --> 00:15:53,960
- [grunting]
- Just look at them go, Father!

310
00:15:54,040 --> 00:15:55,330
Get off of me!

311
00:15:55,420 --> 00:15:57,550
Hey, what is that?

312
00:15:58,510 --> 00:16:00,260
- Inako is flying.
- [gasps]

313
00:16:00,340 --> 00:16:02,760
No way! I wanna see!

314
00:16:03,550 --> 00:16:04,890
[Kinachi trembling]

315
00:16:04,970 --> 00:16:06,510
We're above the smoke clouds.

316
00:16:06,600 --> 00:16:10,020
- I can see all of Kyoto from up here!
- [laughs] It worked!

317
00:16:10,100 --> 00:16:14,060
- We're actually flying!
- We're close enough to touch the clouds!

318
00:16:14,150 --> 00:16:16,400
- Ah, it's beautiful!
- [sniffs]

319
00:16:16,480 --> 00:16:18,650
[joyful music playing]

320
00:16:18,730 --> 00:16:20,730
[Kihachi sniffling]

321
00:16:21,740 --> 00:16:23,410
[wind whistling]

322
00:16:24,160 --> 00:16:26,790
Yeah. It really is beautiful.

323
00:16:27,790 --> 00:16:31,040
- It feels like we could go anywhere.
- Yeah.

324
00:16:32,500 --> 00:16:35,710
[Inako] Hey, Kihachi, 
can you see Mount Fuji over there?

325
00:16:35,790 --> 00:16:36,920
[Kihachi] Mount Fuji?

326
00:16:37,590 --> 00:16:39,510
[Inako] It feels like a dream.

327
00:16:44,050 --> 00:16:45,760
I could fly up here forever--

328
00:16:45,850 --> 00:16:46,890
[screams]

329
00:16:47,350 --> 00:16:49,020
[both screaming]

330
00:16:52,480 --> 00:16:53,400
[Izo] Ah!

331
00:16:53,480 --> 00:16:54,770
Mr. Mizoe!

332
00:16:54,850 --> 00:16:57,890
I have to close the kite.
There's no other way! Ready?

333
00:16:57,980 --> 00:16:59,230
[Inako] Ready!

334
00:17:00,190 --> 00:17:01,530
[grunting]

335
00:17:01,610 --> 00:17:03,490
[both screaming]

336
00:17:05,030 --> 00:17:07,280
- [Kihachi] On the count of three…
- [Inako] 'Kay!

337
00:17:07,369 --> 00:17:08,869
[Kihachi] One, two, three!

338
00:17:08,950 --> 00:17:10,540
[Inako squeals]

339
00:17:10,619 --> 00:17:12,119
[silence]

340
00:17:13,040 --> 00:17:14,960
[Inako and Kihachi screaming]

341
00:17:17,079 --> 00:17:18,829
- [both yelping]
- [branches breaking]

342
00:17:18,920 --> 00:17:20,339
- [Kihachi] Argh!
- [Inako] Ugh!

343
00:17:21,339 --> 00:17:22,550
[both groan]

344
00:17:23,550 --> 00:17:25,930
- [gasps] Are you okay?
- [Kihachi groans]

345
00:17:26,010 --> 00:17:27,800
[gasps] Oh, gimme a break!

346
00:17:28,300 --> 00:17:30,760
Is that Inako up ahead? What's going on?

347
00:17:30,850 --> 00:17:32,940
That boy is kidnapping my fiancée!

348
00:17:33,020 --> 00:17:35,310
He's trying to do what?

349
00:17:35,390 --> 00:17:37,310
[yelling]

350
00:17:38,310 --> 00:17:41,230
[Yosuke] Why did you stop? Circle around
and we'll attack from both sides!

351
00:17:41,320 --> 00:17:42,450
[both panting]

352
00:17:42,530 --> 00:17:43,990
[Inako yelps]

353
00:17:44,070 --> 00:17:45,450
I think I sprained my ankle.

354
00:17:45,530 --> 00:17:47,240
- [Kihachi] Lean on me!
- [Inako whimpers]

355
00:17:48,120 --> 00:17:49,290
- [Kengo roars]
- [Inako gasps]

356
00:17:49,370 --> 00:17:50,250
What's that?

357
00:17:50,330 --> 00:17:52,420
You can't run from me, you filthy punk!

358
00:17:52,500 --> 00:17:54,750
Give Inako back!

359
00:17:54,830 --> 00:17:56,420
[Kihachi] Oh, that guy can't be human!

360
00:17:56,500 --> 00:18:00,050
[Inako] My sister always says Kengo is
as strong and fast as a steam engine.

361
00:18:00,130 --> 00:18:01,670
[Kihachi] He's a human train!

362
00:18:02,340 --> 00:18:04,090
[Kengo yelling]]

363
00:18:07,010 --> 00:18:08,350
[groans]

364
00:18:09,890 --> 00:18:11,890
[sounds slow]

365
00:18:14,390 --> 00:18:15,560
[mother gasps]

366
00:18:17,690 --> 00:18:18,570
[cries]

367
00:18:19,610 --> 00:18:22,240
- [Inako] Quick, this way.
- [Kihachi] Right.

368
00:18:23,110 --> 00:18:24,820
- [yelps] I can't!
- Kihachi?

369
00:18:24,900 --> 00:18:26,440
No, I can't go in there.

370
00:18:26,530 --> 00:18:28,570
It's too dark. I'm afraid of the dark.

371
00:18:28,660 --> 00:18:30,870
It didn't seem
to bother you in the storeroom.

372
00:18:30,950 --> 00:18:33,830
That's because there was still plenty
of natural light in there. [whimpers]

373
00:18:33,910 --> 00:18:35,830
- [Yosuke] Izo! They went this way!
- Huh?

374
00:18:35,910 --> 00:18:37,750
Let's just go back.

375
00:18:37,830 --> 00:18:40,040
[Inako] If we go back, they'll catch you.

376
00:18:40,750 --> 00:18:42,340
- Kihachi.
- [whimpers]

377
00:18:42,420 --> 00:18:43,340
[sighs shakily]

378
00:18:43,920 --> 00:18:46,920
I'll lead the way. Take my hand.

379
00:18:47,930 --> 00:18:49,810
Are you really not afraid of the dark?

380
00:18:49,890 --> 00:18:52,940
I have nothing to fear, 'cause
the Great God Akubi is protecting me!

381
00:18:53,010 --> 00:18:53,930
[Kihachi] Huh?

382
00:18:56,020 --> 00:18:57,110
- [water drips]
- [yelps]

383
00:18:58,350 --> 00:19:01,060
[gasps] They must be hiding in there.

384
00:19:01,150 --> 00:19:04,780
Where is that kidnapping punk?

385
00:19:04,860 --> 00:19:07,280
- [scoffs] The big idiot.
- [Kengo roaring]

386
00:19:07,360 --> 00:19:09,700
Hurry up, Kuga! He's hiding her over here!

387
00:19:10,280 --> 00:19:12,070
- Izo, lend him a hand, would you?
- Right!

388
00:19:13,660 --> 00:19:14,790
- [groans]
- [clattering]

389
00:19:14,870 --> 00:19:16,120
- [thud]
- [both gasp]

390
00:19:16,200 --> 00:19:19,200
I think Kengo found us. We need to go!

391
00:19:20,960 --> 00:19:22,960
[insects chirping]

392
00:19:28,840 --> 00:19:30,050
We made it! [yelps]

393
00:19:31,140 --> 00:19:32,020
[gasps]

394
00:19:32,090 --> 00:19:35,010
You've proven to be
quite a handful, my darling.

395
00:19:35,100 --> 00:19:36,230
Let her go!

396
00:19:36,310 --> 00:19:39,480
I've got you now, you filthy kidnapper.

397
00:19:39,560 --> 00:19:41,190
I didn't kidnap anyone!

398
00:19:41,270 --> 00:19:43,480
No, Kengo, please! You don't understand!

399
00:19:43,560 --> 00:19:45,650
What exactly are we misunderstanding here?

400
00:19:45,730 --> 00:19:48,150
He did try to run off
with my fiancée, after all.

401
00:19:48,240 --> 00:19:51,160
THE 20TH CENTURY ELECTRICAL CATALOG

402
00:19:51,240 --> 00:19:53,410
- [dramatic music playing]
- [Yosuke and Kengo gasp]

403
00:19:54,490 --> 00:19:55,530
[Kihachi gasps]

404
00:19:55,620 --> 00:19:58,660
The 20th Century Electrical Catalog…

405
00:19:58,750 --> 00:20:00,250
[Kihachi shrieks]

406
00:20:01,460 --> 00:20:02,420
This belongs to me!

407
00:20:02,500 --> 00:20:06,300
It's all I have left of my big brother
Seiroku, and I won't let you take it!

408
00:20:06,380 --> 00:20:08,550
You're Seiroku's… brother?

409
00:20:08,630 --> 00:20:12,800
That's right. I'm Kihachi Sakamoto.
Seiroku Sakamoto was my brother!

410
00:20:13,550 --> 00:20:16,300
[snarls] I know precisely who you are.

411
00:20:16,390 --> 00:20:17,730
- [gasps]
- [Yosuke] Izo!

412
00:20:17,810 --> 00:20:19,440
- [Izo] Sir.
- [Yosuke] Let's go, darling.

413
00:20:19,520 --> 00:20:20,900
[Kihachi whimpers]

414
00:20:21,390 --> 00:20:22,810
- [rustling]
- [Inako] Kihachi!

415
00:20:22,900 --> 00:20:24,820
Hey! Get your hands off me!

416
00:20:24,900 --> 00:20:26,070
I must ask you to be still.

417
00:20:26,150 --> 00:20:30,820
Hey! Put me down! I told you already, 
that catalog is mine! Let go of me!

418
00:20:32,320 --> 00:20:33,860
[sighs deeply]

419
00:20:36,910 --> 00:20:38,620
[door slides open]

420
00:20:38,700 --> 00:20:41,410
[Yosuke] Anyone home? Mr. Momokawa?

421
00:20:41,910 --> 00:20:44,000
I've come to return my darling.

422
00:20:46,500 --> 00:20:48,710
- Uh… Inako!
- Inako!

423
00:20:48,800 --> 00:20:50,640
I'm okay, big sister. [winces]

424
00:20:50,710 --> 00:20:52,800
- [Inari squeaking]
- [Noriko] Inako, you're injured!

425
00:20:53,800 --> 00:20:56,260
[servant]Come with me, miss.
I will tend to your leg.

426
00:20:56,350 --> 00:20:57,850
[Inako] Thank you, Tome.

427
00:20:58,810 --> 00:21:00,140
- [thud]
- [Noriko and Inako] Huh?

428
00:21:00,220 --> 00:21:01,760
[footsteps approach]

429
00:21:01,850 --> 00:21:04,350
This is the man
who tried to kidnap your daughter.

430
00:21:05,230 --> 00:21:08,110
[chuckles] I must admit, 
he proved to be quite a handful.

431
00:21:08,190 --> 00:21:11,900
[Mr. Momokawa] I don't understand.
How were you able to track him down?

432
00:21:11,990 --> 00:21:14,490
[Yosuke] I suppose you could call it fate.

433
00:21:16,490 --> 00:21:19,580
- [Noriko] Is that Kihachi Sakamoto?
- It is.

434
00:21:20,080 --> 00:21:24,000
- Trust me, I'm as confused as you are.
- [yelps] Damn it!

435
00:21:24,750 --> 00:21:25,630
[step creaks]

436
00:21:27,670 --> 00:21:28,710
[Izo] Mr. Mizoe.

437
00:21:29,210 --> 00:21:30,340
[gasps]

438
00:21:30,420 --> 00:21:32,130
Mine at last.

439
00:21:32,210 --> 00:21:35,130
You pompous jerk!
That belongs to me and you know it!

440
00:21:35,220 --> 00:21:38,140
[scoffs] You can shout all you want.

441
00:21:38,930 --> 00:21:40,020
[whispers] Seiroku.

442
00:21:40,100 --> 00:21:43,520
At last, I will make our dream a reality.

443
00:21:47,480 --> 00:21:48,360
Huh?

444
00:21:49,060 --> 00:21:51,400
[gasps] Is this a joke?

445
00:21:51,480 --> 00:21:53,900
THE 20TH CENTURY, A NEW ERA--

446
00:21:53,990 --> 00:21:55,160
[Yosuke] No…

447
00:21:55,240 --> 00:21:56,580
[breathing shakily]

448
00:21:57,910 --> 00:21:59,620
This can't be the whole thing.

449
00:22:00,740 --> 00:22:02,910
It's nonsense! It's… it's…

450
00:22:03,000 --> 00:22:05,670
a bunch of kids' drawings!

451
00:22:06,250 --> 00:22:08,840
[Seiroku] This catalog holds
incredible power.

452
00:22:09,500 --> 00:22:10,670
It's a secret!

453
00:22:10,750 --> 00:22:12,960
Impossible! This can't be it!

454
00:22:13,050 --> 00:22:14,090
Oh, I see.

455
00:22:14,170 --> 00:22:16,090
The real catalog must be…

456
00:22:16,180 --> 00:22:18,020
[pages rustling]

457
00:22:18,720 --> 00:22:20,100
- [Yosuke] I'm no fool!
- [both gasp]

458
00:22:20,180 --> 00:22:22,180
[Yosuke panting] This is a fake!

459
00:22:22,260 --> 00:22:23,720
[wheezing]

460
00:22:23,810 --> 00:22:25,400
- [yells]
- [Kihachi gasps]

461
00:22:25,480 --> 00:22:28,110
[Yosuke] I don't know how you did it, 
but this catalog is a fake!

462
00:22:28,190 --> 00:22:30,280
Where is the real one?

463
00:22:30,360 --> 00:22:31,400
[Kihachi gasps]

464
00:22:32,230 --> 00:22:33,860
["Soarin'" by Ginger Root playing]

465
00:22:35,150 --> 00:22:36,690
[Kihachi] It's a fake?

466
00:22:51,090 --> 00:22:54,800
♪ Looking up and within ♪

467
00:22:54,880 --> 00:22:57,050
♪ To try and move forward ♪

468
00:22:57,130 --> 00:23:01,010
♪ Get back what you gave in ♪

469
00:23:01,100 --> 00:23:02,850
♪ To drag yourself in ♪

470
00:23:02,930 --> 00:23:05,560
[lyrics in Japanese]

471
00:23:05,640 --> 00:23:08,430
♪ Oh, I'll be waitin' ♪

472
00:23:09,140 --> 00:23:11,060
[lyrics in Japanese]

473
00:23:19,150 --> 00:23:23,660
♪ Look at how far we've come ♪

474
00:23:23,740 --> 00:23:27,370
♪All together ♪

475
00:23:27,450 --> 00:23:30,790
♪ Soarin' ♪

476
00:23:31,420 --> 00:23:33,420
[lyrics in Japanese]

477
00:23:35,800 --> 00:23:37,470
♪ When I'm with you ♪

478
00:23:37,970 --> 00:23:42,890
♪ Somethin' tells me I'm gonna be alone ♪
